WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.490
Before the first session, set
up each laptop or tablet once.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.700
Here's how.

3
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.470
Open thinkerwell.app, tap For educators,

4
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:10.970
then Set up this device.

5
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.430
The checklist says which steps
are already done on this device.

6
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.790
First, add Thinkerwell to the home screen,

7
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.530
so it opens like an app.

8
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.410
The checklist shows the steps
for your kind of device.

9
00:00:22.668 --> 00:00:26.470
On an iPad, this also stops
Safari deleting saved work.

10
00:00:27.506 --> 00:00:29.590
Then open Thinkerwell from its icon,

11
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.630
with the internet on, and keep it
open while the lessons are saved.

12
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.150
After that, every lesson works offline.

13
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.830
Next, tap Keep work safe, so the
browser keeps learners' work,

14
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.490
even when space runs low.

15
00:00:43.527 --> 00:00:45.370
Add the learners who use the device.

16
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.770
Each one gets a tile on the home page.

17
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.410
Using code cards? Learners
type their code as their name.

18
00:00:52.431 --> 00:00:55.850
In Settings, you can choose the
voice that reads lessons aloud.

19
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.380
Do the speech check last: under Say it,

20
00:00:58.420 --> 00:00:59.670
tap Check this device.

21
00:01:00.803 --> 00:01:03.130
Before you reset a device or give it back,

22
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.960
save everyone's work to a file,

23
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.850
and load it on the next one.

24
00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.590
The checklist prints on one page,

25
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.310
so you can tick it off on paper.

26
00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.420
Thinkerwell.

27
00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.640
Social studies and beyond.

